<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - British Petroleum up.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - British Petroleum up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc was up in preopen trade but traders said that U.S. oil stocks had not so far reacted to the U.S. missile attack in Iraq.</p>
<p>Traders said that British Petroleum was traded at 118-3/4, after having closed at 117-3/4 on the New York Stock Exchange last Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been kind of slow this morning,&quot; one trader said. &quot;There is nothing going on in Texaco (Inc), Exxon (Corp) or Mobil (Corp).&quot;</p>
</text>
